# ============================================================
#  The Midnight Cartographers, expanded (threads 1, docs/threads-1-plan.md Part E).
#  - The Master Map (a quest thread): Corvin, its new Keeper, shows a member the map's two great blanks. Draw two
#    lines on it (either blank, or a blank and the shortcut found inside it) and he asks you to keep it with him.
#    Two of the blanks open the midnight heists: the stair below the chained shelf (`heist_stacks_known`, lead
#    lead_deep_stacks; content/events/heists/stacks.grim) and the seventh tower's wall stair (`heist_tower_known`,
#    lead lead_tower_stair; heists/tower.grim). Once a blank is filled, a shortcut inside it can be charted
#    (`carto_book_lift`, `carto_tower_chimney`). None of it touches the main plot: the tower blank is the wall, and the
#    chimney comes out among the old classrooms, well below the top room.
#  - Routine society cards (drawn at the third gargoyle, like the club's others) and two midnight cards there.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- The Master Map (quest) ----------------

@thread carto_master_map
from: quest
with: begun=carto_map_chain
when: turn >= 8
track: cartographers
clues: lead_master_map lead_deep_stacks lead_tower_stair
name: The Master Map
premise: The Cartographers' Master Map has two great blanks nobody has filled in thirty years. Draw two lines there, and Corvin will ask you to keep the map with him.
journal:
  flag(carto_map_chain): Corvin unrolled the Master Map and showed you its two great blanks. "Two lines on it," he said, "and you keep it with me."
  flag(heist_stacks_known): You charted the stair under the last chained shelf, down to the deep stacks and the confiscation vault.
  flag(heist_tower_known): You found the seventh tower's second stair, inside the wall, from the cellars to the landing of candles.
  flag(carto_book_lift): You rode the old book-lift down its shaft, from the bindery deep into the stacks, to where the shelves start breathing.
  flag(carto_tower_chimney): You climbed the seventh tower's old chimney from the cellars and came out in a classroom a floor above the landing of candles.
  flag(carto_map_keeper): Corvin put the Master Map in your hands. You keep it together now.
  flag(carto_map_done) and not flag(carto_map_keeper): You told Corvin to keep the map himself. He looked relieved.
status:
  resolved: flag(carto_map_done)
members:
  start carto_map_blanks
  part carto_deep_stacks flag=heist_stacks_known
  part carto_tower_stair flag=heist_tower_known
  part carto_book_lift flag=carto_book_lift
  part carto_tower_chimney flag=carto_tower_chimney
  final carto_map_keeper

@event carto_map_blanks
title: The Blanks on the Map
thread: carto_master_map
class: routine
tone: eerie
when: member(cartographers)
actor: corvin
art: map
tags: club mystery
scene: A huge map in shifting silver ink spread on the stone floor of a secret passage, weighted with candle stubs, two regions of it completely blank.
text: {seen(carto_map_blanks) > 1: Corvin has the Master Map out again, and the two blanks are still white as snow. "Still thirty years," he says. "Still yours if you want them."|Corvin has the Master Map out on the passage floor, weighted with candle stubs: silver lines that move a little, like breathing, and two great blanks. One is under the library, below the last chained shelf; one is inside the seventh tower's wall. "The last Keeper left it to me this summer," he says. "Two lines on those, and you keep it with me. Fancy it?"}
> left: "Show me where to start."
  flag carto_map_chain
  find lead_master_map
  guile +tiny
  say: Corvin grins and rolls the map to the library end. "The chained shelf, then," he says. "Bring chalk. Don't touch the chains."
  chain_beat = turn
  queue carto_deep_stacks now
> right: "Not this year."
  rel corvin -tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: {seen(carto_map_blanks) > 1: "One day," says Corvin, and rolls it up without a joke this time.|"Thirty-one years, then," says Corvin, and rolls the map up a little too neatly.}

@event carto_deep_stacks
title: The Stair Under the Chained Shelf
thread: carto_master_map
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: book
tags: club mystery danger
scene: The bottom shelf of a dark library aisle, iron chains running from the books down through holes in the floorboards, a student kneeling with a stub of chalk.
text: Below the east stacks' last chained shelf in the Restricted Section, by the book-return hatch, the Master Map simply stops. The chains on that shelf run down through the floor, and at night something below pulls them taut. Corvin's way in is a book-return hatch nobody has locked since it was built. The shelf is yours to chart.
> left: Find the stair and pace it down
  challenge research using guile journeyman:
    win:
      flag heist_stacks_known
      find lead_deep_stacks
      guile +small
      say: Behind the shelf's kickboard, a stair goes down forty-four steps, between shelves that breathe in their sleep, to stacks no lamp reaches. At the bottom is a door with a prefects' padlock: the confiscation vault. You chart it all, and come up very quietly.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: You find the stair, and it turns more times than it has steps. You come up in the same aisle you went down from, with your chalk worn to nothing and the chains above you swinging.
  next
> right: Copy what the old margins say
  lore +small
  say: The oldest map in the club has a note in the margin by the chained shelf, in brown ink: "Stair: yes. Down: no. Ask the chains." You copy it out neatly. The blank stays blank.

@event carto_tower_stair
title: Two Strides Fatter
thread: carto_master_map
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: door
tags: club mystery
scene: A student in a dark vaulted cellar pressing an ear to a curved stone wall, a candle and a coil of measuring string at their feet.
text: The seventh tower's blank on the Master Map isn't its own stair, locked as it is; that's on every old plan. It's the wall. Corvin has measured the tower from outside and from in, and the outside is two strides fatter. "There's a second stair in there," he says. "A servants' stair, from the cellars up. Find its door."
> left: Sound the cellar walls
  challenge research using guile journeyman:
    win:
      flag heist_tower_known
      find lead_tower_stair
      guile +small
      say: Behind a rack of empty bottles, one stone rings hollow. The door behind it opens on a stair one shoulder wide, curling up inside the wall. You follow it to a loose panel that comes out on the landing of candles, halfway up, and nobody on the main stair any the wiser.
    lose:
      mood -small
      health -tiny
      say: You knock on stone until your knuckles are raw and every wall in the cellar sounds the same. The tower keeps its two strides to itself, for now.
  next
> right: Measure it again from outside
  lore +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: You walk the tower's foot in the cold with Corvin's string, and get the same answer he did: two strides. Your fingers are numb and the blank is still blank, but now you believe in it.

@event carto_book_lift
title: The Book-Lift
thread: carto_master_map
class: routine
tone: tense
when: flag(heist_stacks_known)
art: book
tags: club mystery danger
scene: A dusty wooden box on a rope inside a narrow shaft, an old library bindery around it, a student climbing into the box with a candle.
text: Under the library, the bindery has an old book-lift: a wooden box on a rope in a shaft, from the days when the stacks went deeper than anyone now admits. The rope is new. Somebody still uses it.
> left: Ride it down
  challenge feat apprentice+:
    win:
      flag carto_book_lift
      guile +tiny
      vigor +tiny
      say: The box lowers you in the dark past floor after floor of shelves, and stops where the shelves start breathing, so gently it might know you. A quicker way down than any stair. You ink the shaft onto the map before you've stopped shaking.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: The rope slips a yard, then another, then catches. You climb out at the first floor down with skinned palms and a new respect for whoever oils it.
  next
> right: Find out who oils the rope
  charm +tiny
  say: Nobody in the bindery will say. Footnote, the library cat, sits by the shaft all afternoon, as if waiting for a lift that never comes.

@event carto_tower_chimney
title: Wide as a Coffin
thread: carto_master_map
class: routine
tone: tense
when: flag(heist_tower_known)
art: door
tags: club mystery danger
scene: A student wedged inside a narrow soot-black chimney, climbing with back and feet, a lantern hung from their belt lighting the brick above.
text: The old classrooms in the seventh tower each had a fireplace, and the fireplaces share one chimney, which starts in the cellar beside your wall stair. A Cartographer fifty years gone wrote in the margin beside it: "Chimney: wide as a coffin. Climbable. Don't."
> left: Climb it
  challenge feat apprentice+:
    win:
      flag carto_tower_chimney
      vigor +tiny
      guile +tiny
      say: Back against one side, feet against the other, soot to the elbows. You come out of a classroom grate a floor above the landing of candles, past the wall stair's slow part, and sit in a century of dust laughing quietly.
    lose:
      health -small
      mood -tiny
      say: Halfway up the chimney narrows, and so do you, and for a long minute neither of you gives. You come down the way you went up, black from head to foot.
  next
> right: Send a lantern up on a cord
  lore +tiny
  say: The lantern goes up and up and comes back sooty, swinging. The margin was right about the coffin.

@event carto_map_keeper
title: The Keeping of the Map
thread: carto_master_map
tone: warm
actor: corvin
art: map
tags: club
scene: A circle of students with candles in a secret passage, one of them holding out a rolled map in silver ink to another.
text: The Cartographers gather round the Master Map with candles. {(flag(heist_stacks_known) and (flag(heist_tower_known) or flag(carto_book_lift))) or (flag(heist_tower_known) and flag(carto_tower_chimney)): Where the blanks were, your lines are, faintly silver and not quite settled.|The blanks are still mostly blank, but the club has watched you try. "Close enough is a Cartographer's whole trade," says Corvin.} "The club says you keep it with me. There's a test. There's always a test. Walk from here to the Thursday stair with the map in your head and no candle."
> left: Walk it in the dark
  challenge research using guile adept- +1 if flag(heist_stacks_known) +1 if flag(heist_tower_known) +1 if flag(carto_book_lift) +1 if flag(carto_tower_chimney):
    win:
      flag carto_map_done carto_map_keeper
      guile +small
      rel corvin +small
      mood +small
      say: You walk it blind, every turning where the map says it is, and at the foot of the Thursday stair the club is waiting with candles. Corvin puts the rolled map in your hands. "Keepers," he says, and for once he doesn't laugh after.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: Three turnings in, the castle moves one. You walk into a wall, very gently, in the dark, and stand there until someone comes with a candle. "It wants more of you," says Corvin kindly. "Come back."
> right: "It's yours, Corvin. Keep it."
  flag carto_map_done
  rel corvin +medium
  say: Corvin looks at you for a long moment, then rolls the map back up and tucks it into his coat, where it has lived since the summer. He looks relieved, and then embarrassed about looking relieved.

# ---------------- The society's other nights (track: cartographers) ----------------

@event carto_forged_map
title: A Map for Sale
track: cartographers
class: routine
tone: light
art: map
tags: club money
scene: A first-year in a corridor selling folded paper maps from a satchel to a small crowd of younger students.
text: A first-year is selling "the secret map of the castle" in the corridor for a crown a copy. It is a forgery, and a good one, and every passage on it leads, by a lovely roundabout way, straight to the prefects' office. Corvin swears it wasn't him.
> left: Let it sell
  guile +tiny
  mood +small
  alignment -tiny
  say: You get a copy for the club's wall. All week first-years turn up, breathless, at the prefects' door. The prefects are delighted. Nobody looks behind the third gargoyle at all.
> right: Buy up the stock and burn it
  gold -small
  alignment +tiny
  say: You buy the whole satchel and burn it in the passage grate. The first-year is thrilled with the money. Somewhere, the forger is very annoyed.

@event carto_quiet_prefect
title: The Prefect Who Doesn't Look
track: cartographers
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: lantern
tags: club
scene: A senior prefect with a lantern on a windy parapet at night, standing beside a gargoyle and not looking at it, talking to a student in the shadows.
text: A senior prefect walks the north parapet on her rounds and never once looks at the third gargoyle. This time she stops beside it, still not looking. "The draught behind this one's got worse," she says to the dark. "Tell whoever needs telling. And somebody's been eating the grapes in the dish. Those were mine."
> left: Trade a shortcut for her rota
  flag prefect_rota
  guile +tiny
  rel corvin -tiny
  say: You give her the back way from the parapet to the prefects' common room, four minutes quicker. She gives you, without a word, the times of every round on her rota. Corvin, when he hears, says giving routes away is how clubs end.
> right: Play dumb
  mood +tiny
  say: "Draught?" you say. "What gargoyle?" She almost smiles, and walks on, swinging the lantern. You keep the club's secrets, and she keeps hers.

@event carto_member_out
title: One Map Fewer
track: cartographers
class: routine
tone: grim
art: map
tags: club
scene: Two students kneeling by a small grate in a stone passage, a stack of hand-drawn maps between them, one holding a lit match.
text: One of the club's seniors has been caught twice this term, and wants out before a third. The club's rule is that leavers burn their maps. She has a year of them in a bundle, and she asks you to sit with her while she does it. "Or hide them," she says. "I can't watch them go."
> left: Burn them with her
  mood -small
  alignment +tiny
  say: You feed the grate one map at a time and she reads each one aloud before it goes. At the end she thanks you, and goes up to bed a member of nothing, and lighter.
> right: Keep them for the club
  guile +small
  queue night_suspicion chance slim
  say: You hide the bundle in the passage where only the club will find it, which means carrying a caught-twice member's maps through the castle after curfew. She doesn't ask where. She'll know, every time she passes the gargoyle, that she didn't really leave.

@event carto_recruit
title: Your Turn to Invite
track: cartographers
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  pick: any where met(pick) and tagged(pick, student) and not npc_is(corvin)
art: map
tags: club social
scene: A black card with a silver map drawn on it being slid under a dormitory door in a dark corridor.
text: Corvin hands you a black card, blank but for a silver line that wanders. "Members bring members," he says. "Your turn. Who?" You think of {pick} before he's finished asking.
> left: Slip it under {pick}'s door
  rel pick +small
  queue night_suspicion chance slim
  say: You slide the card under {pick}'s door at midnight and run. Three nights later {pick} comes in under the gargoyle with a candle and a look you'll remember: someone finding out the castle is bigger than they thought.
> right: "Nobody I'd trust with it."
  rel corvin -tiny
  guile +tiny
  say: Corvin takes the card back. "Careful's a good thing in a Cartographer," he says, and doesn't sound as if he means it.

# ---------------- The third gargoyle at midnight ----------------

@event gargoyle_midnight_one_short
title: One Short
pool: gargoyle_passage_routine
slot: midnight
tone: tense
repeat: 4
weight: 10
art: lantern
tags: club danger
scene: A huddle of students with candles in a dark stone passage, one of them counting heads, an empty gap in the circle.
text: Midnight under the gargoyle, and the headcount comes up one short. {~Someone went into the passages alone an hour ago, to settle a bet about a stair that only goes down on wet nights.|Someone took a dare about the kitchens' dumbwaiter, and the dare was "alone".|A new member, it turns out, sleepwalks, and nodded off on the bench an hour ago, and the bench is empty.} Nobody says anything for a moment.
> left: Go after them
  challenge feat using guile journeyman:
    win:
      guile +small
      mood +small
      say: {~You find them two floors down, on a step that wasn't there yesterday and can't now be got off. You talk them down one stride at a time.|You find them stuck in the dumbwaiter between two floors, very glad of company. You wind them down by the rope, slowly, and walk them back.|You find them on the parapet, asleep on their feet and walking the edge. You turn them round by the shoulders, gently, and walk them home.}
    lose:
      health -small
      queue night_suspicion chance unlikely
      say: {~The passages turn you round twice, and a prefect's lantern turns you round a third time. The missing member gets back on their own at dawn, grinning.|You never find the dumbwaiter's shaft, and a prefect nearly finds you. They come back at dawn, floury and triumphant.|You search every passage but the right one. At dawn they wake in their own bed, with no idea anyone looked.}
> right: Wait with the others
  mood -small
  say: {~You sit in the circle with the gap in it, and at dawn they climb back out of the wall, filthy and triumphant. The waiting was worse than going.|At dawn they come back through the wall, floury to the elbows, with a story nobody believes. The waiting was worse than going.|At dawn somebody finds them asleep in the library. The waiting was worse than going.}

@event gargoyle_midnight_lost_map
title: A Map on the Wrong Table
pool: gargoyle_passage_routine
slot: midnight
tone: tense
repeat: 4
weight: 8
art: map
tags: club danger
scene: A dark common room with red sashes hung over chairs, a folded hand-drawn map lying on a table in a pool of moonlight.
text: {~A second-year Cartographer dropped their copy of the kitchens' passages, and it's turned up on a table in the prefects' common room.|One of the club's old route maps, the one to the boathouse, is lying on the prefects' study desk, where a cleaner left it.|A first-year member lent their map to a friend, and the friend lost it to a prefect's coat pocket, and the coat is hanging in the prefects' common room.} Nobody has opened it yet. It's still there at midnight.
> left: Steal it back
  challenge deceive journeyman:
    win:
      guile +small
      mood +tiny
      say: {~In through the door, across the moonlit rug, map into your shirt, out. A prefect turns over in an armchair by the fire and doesn't wake.|You lift it off the desk between two snores. The club has it back by one o'clock.|You go through the coat's pockets in the dark, find the map and a toffee, and take only the map.}
    lose:
      mood -small
      queue night_suspicion now
      say: {~You get the map, and a prefect gets a very good look at you holding it. You run. The map is safe; you aren't, quite.|A floorboard by the desk squeaks. You get out with the map and a prefect's voice behind you, asking your name.|The coat's owner comes back for it while your hand's in the pocket. You run, map and all, and they know your face.}
> right: Redraw the routes instead
  lore +tiny
  mood -small
  say: {~The club spends the night changing every route to the kitchens: new chalk, new turnings, a passage given up for good.|The club gives up the old boathouse route for good, and spends the night finding a worse one.|The club spends the night redrawing everything the lost map showed. By dawn it's worth nothing to anyone.}
